       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nAcetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day. The usual adult maximum is 4 g/day, and many institutions cap it at 3 g/day. A single 5000 mg dose is also well above the normal maximum single dose of 1000 mg. At this level there is a serious risk of hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **500 mg** PO three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg** PO three times daily (1.95 g/day)\n- **1000 mg** PO three times daily (3 g/day)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If 5000 mg really is what you intended, please confirm that. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
