     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 15 g/day is a toxic dose. A single 5 g dose is already in the range where acute liver injury is a concern, and I know of no indication for it. Three of those doses a day would very likely cause serious harm to the patient.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can enter 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day) or 650 mg PO every 6 hours right now. Just tell me which.\n- **Check with pharmacy or your attending.** If you have a reason for the higher dose, they can review it. Any order that exceeds the maximum would also need to go through your institution's override process.\n- **Consider a suspected overdose.** If this is for an acetaminophen ingestion, treatment is N-acetylcysteine guided by a serum level. Poison Control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) can help, and I can enter that order if you want.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
     ],
